.Dd November 4, 2026
.Dt PAM_XDG 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm pam_xdg
.Nd manage an XDG runtime directory for a PAM session
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Op Ar service-name
.Ar session control-flag
.Pa pam_xdg.so
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
module creates a private per-user runtime directory below
.Pa /var/run/xdg ,
sets
.Ev XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
in the PAM environment, and removes the directory when the last tracked session
closes.
.Pp
The root-owned control directory
.Pa /var/run/xdg-control
has mode 0700; the root-owned runtime parent
.Pa /var/run/xdg
has mode 0711.  Each user directory is owned by its user and group and has
mode 0700 and is named by numeric user ID.
Existing directories with unexpected owners or modes are rejected.
.Pp
Cleanup refuses to descend into mounted filesystems or directories owned by
another user.
.Pp
The PAM session owner must retain its PAM handle until session close.
.Pp
Session locks are released when a process exits.  Stale sessions are recovered
when the next session for the user opens; an abnormal exit alone does not cause
immediate directory removal.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr pam 3 ,
.Xr pam.conf 5
